  "title": "Battle of Zama",
  "summary": "In 202 BCE a Roman army under Scipio Africanus defeated the Carthaginian army of Hannibal near Zama, about 97 km southwest of Carthage. Hannibal fielded 80 elephants; Polybius reported about 20,000 Carthaginian and 1,500 Roman dead. Carthage later accepted harsh peace terms.",
